Iran,IRN,"Can non-violent effects alone qualify as “force” (e.g., substantial economic harm, losses of functionality, etc.)?",No,"Armed forces of the Islamic Republic of Iran believe that certainly, those cyber operations resulting in material damage to property and/or persons in the widespread and grave manner and or it logically is probable to result in such implications constitutes use of force. Should such operations affect the vital national infrastructures, including defensive infrastructures- whether owned by the public or private sector- they shall violate the principle of the non-use of force.","Iran Cyber Statement (2020) Art. IV, Pt. 1",,
